{"page_id": "docparsing_images-images_8e1dd51f_images_manufacturing_operation_sop_00004-p1", "markdown": "CLASS 5 Series: AC X1Y1 & X1Y2\n\nROHS\n\nINTERNATIONAL\n\n• HOW TO ORDER\n\n5-KL F 472 M AC2K5 10 Y 5 (1) (2)\n\n(3) (4)\n\n(6) (7) (8)\n\n1. Type Code: KL class X1-Y2 ; WD class X1-Y1\n\n2. Temperature Characteristic: Temp.\n\nCode\n\nc\n\nCoefficient COG SL\n\nCode\n\nTemp. Coefficient YSP X7R\n\nCode\n\nTemp. Coefficient YSU Y5V\n\n3. Capacitance Code: Expressed by three-digit alphanumeric. The unit is pico-farad (pF). The first and second figures are significant digits, and the third figure expresses the number of zeros which follow the two numbers. If there is a decimal point in between first two figures, it is expressed by the capital letter \"R\". See below examples: Code\n\nCapacitance\n\nCode\n\nCapacitance\n\n5R1\n\n5.1 pF\n\n100\n\n10 pF\n\n8RO\n\n8 pF\n\n101\n\n100 pF\n\nCode 472 103\n\nCapacitance 4700 pF 0.1 uF\n\n4. Capacitance Tolerance Code Code\n\nTolerance\n\nCode\n\n+ 0.25pF 土0.50pF\n\nTolerance * 5% 土10％\n\nCode\n\n5. Minimum Test Voltage (AC) : X1Y2 = AC2K5, X1Y1 = AC4KV 6. Lead Spacing (F) Code\n\nCode\n\nTolerance * 20% +80/-20%\n\nLead spacing (F) 5.020.8mm 6.35+0.8mm\n\n10\n\nLead spacing (F) 7.5:0.8mm 10.0+0.8mm\n\n7. Lead style\n\nCode\n\nY\n\nLead Style\n\n8. Lead length & package style: Omitted for un-cut bulk pack or Code L 5 = 5+/-1mm, bulk pack, 6 = 6+/-1mm ... etc. (cut leads only available in bulk pack) A = Taped & Ammo pack, R = Taped & on Reel\n\nRFE International • Tel (949) 833-1988 • Fax (949) 833-1788 • E-mail sales@rfeinc.com Page 3 of 8\n\n21NJUL-2023", "width": 595, "height": 810, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "CLASS 5 Series: AC X1Y1 & X1Y2", "bbox": {"x": 163.7, "y": 44.0, "width": 293.5, "height": 16.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "ROHS", "bbox": {"x": 531.1, "y": 36.0, "width": 26.0, "height": 10.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "INTERNATIONAL", "bbox": {"x": 51.9, "y": 62.0, "width": 113.79999999999998, "height